ts that\n  - publish twice and check that the second item is stored with a `Decimal`\n    score,\n  - publish three stories through `handler()` and expect 201 each time,\n  - check that `to_dynamo` converts nested floats.\n\n  `FakeTable` rejects floats the same way boto3 does. The new tests fail on the\n  old code (1 failure, 2 errors) and pass with the fix\n  (`python3 -m unittest discover tests` → 4 tests OK).\n\nNote: the stories already in production are fine. The first story has\n`similar: []`, and the failed publishes wrote nothing. Stories published before\nthe fix won't list stories published after them as related, because `similar`\nis computed only once, when a story is published. That's how the design already\nworks, not something this bug caused.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AYbw9ntNdrxZWU6BLmqYXc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENkKwa2Unb6HA1N3oMi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because the item it tries to save contains plain Python decimal numbers (floats), and boto3 won't send floats to DynamoDB. It raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`, and the handler turns that into a 500. I've fixed it, and the new tests pass (4 of 4).\n\n**Why only the second time:** each story is saved with similarity scores against the stories already in the table. On the first publish the table was empty, so there were no scores and nothing to reject (the log shows `similar=0 stored`). From the second publish on, every save contains scores and fails.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** I added `to_dynamo()`, which converts every float in the item to `Decimal`. `publish()` runs the whole item through it right before saving. Because it covers the whole item at the one place it's written, a number field added later (another score or ratio, say) is converted too.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** the only existing test published one story into an empty table, so it never hit this. I added tests that:\n  - publish twice and check the second item is stored with a `Decimal` score;\n  - publish three stories through the handler and expect a 201 each time;\n  - check that floats nested inside the item are converted.\n\n  On the old code the new tests fail (1 failure, 2 errors); with the fix all 4 pass.\n\n**Existing data:** nothing needs cleaning up. The first story was saved with an empty related list, and the failed publishes wrote nothing. The one limit is how the service already works: related stories are worked out only when a story is published, so older stories won't list newer ones as related.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the cause and the fix written out. Nothing is committed or deployed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_